raw_answer:
I could not successfully execute a robust final SPARQL query because repeated attempts to run the final query against the DBpedia QLever endpoint timed out. I did run simpler queries earlier which returned the directors for both films and showed Roland West has dbo:deathDate = 1952-03-31; Frank Stauffacher did not have dbo:deathDate but his DBpedia abstract/comment contains the death date 24 July 1955. Based on those results the director of De Luxe Annie (Roland West, died 1952) died earlier than the director of Notes on the Port of St. Francis (Frank Stauffacher, died 1955).

Below is my best attempt at a final SPARQL query that (1) pulls structured deathDate where present, (2) extracts a day-month-year death date from the English abstract when necessary, (3) computes a death year and orders by it so the film with the director who died earliest is first. I could not successfully execute this query due to endpoint timeouts.

Best attempt SPARQL:

PREFIX dbo: <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/>
PREFIX dbr: <http://dbpedia.org/resource/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?film ?filmLabel ?director ?directorLabel ?deathDate ?deathYear WHERE {
  VALUES ?film { dbr:Notes_on_the_Port_of_St._Francis dbr:De_Luxe_Annie }
  ?film dbo:director ?director .
  OPTIONAL { ?director dbo:deathDate ?deathDate . BIND(YEAR(?deathDate) AS ?deathYearFromDate) }
  OPTIONAL {
    ?director dbo:abstract ?abs FILTER(lang(?abs) = "en") .
    # extract a day-month-year pattern (e.g. "24 July 1955") from the abstract
    BIND(REPLACE(STR(?abs), '.*(\\d{1,2}\\s+[A-Za-z]+\\s+\\d{4}).*', '$1') AS ?deathDMY)
    BIND(xsd:integer(REPLACE(STR(?deathDMY), '.*(\\d{4}).*', '$1')) AS ?deathYearFromAbstract)
  }
  BIND(COALESCE(?deathYearFromDate, ?deathYearFromAbstract) AS ?deathYear)
  OPTIONAL { ?film rdfs:label ?filmLabel FILTER(lang(?filmLabel) = "en") }
  OPTIONAL { ?director rdfs:label ?directorLabel FILTER(lang(?directorLabel) = "en") }
}
ORDER BY ?deathYear

Note: if executed successfully, the query should return the film whose director died earliest as the first row (ORDER BY ?deathYear LIMIT 1 would return only that film).

